# product/connector/.env.example
#
# Authoritative env surface for the @swoop/connector service. Copy to
# product/connector/.env (gitignored) and fill in any values that should
# differ from the defaults.
#
# Schema: product/connector/src/config/schema.ts. Validation runs at
# boot — a malformed value fails fast with a Zod error pointing at the
# offending field. See gotchas.md ("Local Postgres is Postgres.app v18…")
# for the bootstrap walkthrough.

# --- Postgres connection -----------------------------------------------------
# Local dev: Postgres.app v18 + puma_dev (per gotchas.md).
# Validation: scheme MUST be postgres:// or postgresql:// AND the path MUST
# include a non-empty database name (single segment). Boot rejects anything
# else — the validation pattern matches the Sec-3 fix at be9ca95 for
# entryUrl.
# Prod (post-M4): Cloud SQL via Cloud SQL Auth Proxy / Unix socket; URL
# fed in via Secret Manager.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://al:pick-a-password@localhost:5432/puma_dev

# --- HTTP server -------------------------------------------------------------
# :3002 stays out of the way of the orchestrator's stub at :3001 (still
# backing the orchestrator until B.t3a swaps it in C.t4) and the UI's
# :5173. Port flips when the stub retires.
CONNECTOR_PORT=3002

# Address the connector HTTP server binds to. Default 127.0.0.1 (loopback only)
# so the connector is not reachable from outside the host without an explicit
# override. Set to 0.0.0.0 only where it must be reachable across the network
# (e.g. the orchestrator runs on a different host).
# CONNECTOR_HOST=127.0.0.1

# --- Postgres pool tunables --------------------------------------------------
# Conservative defaults per the C.t1 HITL ratification (Q1). Surfaced as
# tunable; revisit at C.t8 runbook authoring + first M4 load test. ETL
# paths (C.t3 / C.t3a) may want a larger PG_POOL_MAX or a different
# statement timeout — that's a per-connection override inside their batch
# transactions, not a service-wide flip.
PG_POOL_MAX=10
PG_POOL_IDLE_MS=30000
PG_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT_MS=10000

# --- Content paths (resolved against the package root at boot) ---------------
# One folder per tool with a `description.md` inside — the authoritative MCP
# tool-description copy, loaded fail-fast at boot (C.t4 / C.34: boot fails if
# any tool's description.md is missing or empty). Mirrors the orchestrator's
# TOOLS_PROMPT_DIR.
# Default: ../cms/prompts/tools
# TOOLS_PROMPT_DIR=../cms/prompts/tools

# Memory tool descriptions (tools/<name>.md), loaded at boot and registered
# with the MCP server (T3-3 relocation).
# Default: ../cms/prompts/memory
# MEMORY_PROMPT_DIR=../cms/prompts/memory

# --- Gemini embeddings (visitor-query vectorisation) -------------------------
# gemini-embedding-001 / halfvec(3072), matching the corpus storage shape
# (decision C.46). The connector embeds visitor utterances into a search vector
# at query time. Optional at boot so the connector starts without it; vector
# retrieval primitives throw a typed error if it's missing at call time (tests
# inject their own embedder and never touch this). Enable the Generative
# Language API on the GCP project + generate an AI Studio key.
# (Note: @swoop/ingestion's embed pass also reads this key from this .env.)
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# --- Pricing data capture date (C.goofy-goldstine-4) -------------------------
# ISO date the source pricing data was captured from the Swoop CMS. Stamped on
# every get_pricing response so the agent + visitor know how fresh the figures
# are. Default 2026-04-27 (the SQL-dump date); bump it when a fresh dump lands.
# PRICES_CAPTURED_AT=2026-04-27

# --- Staff JWT secret (sm-t2-auth hardening) ---------------------------------
# When set, the connector cryptographically verifies incoming staff JWTs
# (issuer / audience / algorithm / signature) rather than the presence-only
# backstop. Must be >= 32 chars AND must match the orchestrator's
# STAFF_JWT_SECRET — a mismatch rejects every staff memory mutation with a
# signature failure. Optional in dev (omit for the presence backstop); required
# in production. Treat like a secret; never log it.
# STAFF_JWT_SECRET=

# --- Environment -------------------------------------------------------------
# One of: development | test | production.
NODE_ENV=development

# --- Observability sink (F-c — planning/03-exec-observability-c.md) ----------
# Where emitted events land:
#   stdout         one JSON line per event (default; dev).
#   postgres       durable INSERT into event_log (migration 020) using the
#                  DATABASE_URL pool above — SQL-queryable today, demo Mini incl.
#   cloud-logging  severity-tagged structured stdout for Cloud Logging +
#                  Error Reporting (Swoop GCP, via Cloud Run / Ops Agent).
# EVENT_SINK=stdout

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Additional vars read by sibling tooling that loads this .env
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# NOT part of the connector service's validated surface — config/schema.ts does
# not define these and silently ignores them. They live here because these
# sibling processes load product/connector/.env and read them via process.env.
#
# @swoop/ingestion — ETL / enrichment CLIs (etl:sql, enrich, annotate-images),
# which load this .env for DATABASE_URL + GEMINI_API_KEY and also read:
#   ENRICH_BUDGET_GBP   hard cost cap (GBP) for the enrich pass. Dev default 10,
#                       prod target 15. Per-run override: --budget-gbp.
#   GEMINI_BATCH_SIZE   docs per Gemini embed batch. Default 100. Lower it
#                       (e.g. 50) to dodge Gemini's sub-second TPM burst 429s.
#   GEMINI_CONCURRENCY  max in-flight embed batches. Default 4. Drop to 1
#                       alongside GEMINI_BATCH_SIZE on a first/large run.
# ENRICH_BUDGET_GBP=10
# GEMINI_BATCH_SIZE=100
# GEMINI_CONCURRENCY=4
#
# Retention-sweep CLI (npm run sweep:handoffs --workspace @swoop/connector):
#   HANDOFF_STORE_DIR   absolute path to the var/handoffs/ directory. Defaults
#                       to <orchestrator-package-root>/var/handoffs to match the
#                       orchestrator's wiring out of the box.
#   HANDOFF_RETENTION_{QUALIFIED,REFERRED_OUT,DISQUALIFIED,INCONCLUSIVE}_WINDOW_SECONDS
#                       per-verdict retention override (seconds). Unset = the
#                       compliance-bundle defaults. For the §5b smoke (1-second
#                       windows) + ad-hoc inspection; production never sets them.
# HANDOFF_STORE_DIR=
